  "final_message": "The audit log key for `service.checkout(\"7781\")` is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nThe call path:\n\n1. `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` in `audit.py`.\n2. `write_audit` sets the key with `_format_key(kind, ident)` at `audit.py:11`.\n3. `_format_key` builds `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`. `AUDIT_PREFIX` is `\"AUD\"` in `config.py`, so the result is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nThe `key =[REDACTED:SECRET]'order', '7781')`, which returned `{'AUD-ORDER-7781': True}`. `decoy_metrics.py` builds keys the same way but with the `MET` prefix, and it never writes to the audit log.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
